All of my speed comparisons basically assume BoS, so yes. On a warhorse 
or other creature with speed 24, you move two moves per turn counter 
tick (vs 5/3 moves with BoS). On a Jabberwock (base speed 15) you can 
use a wand of speed monster to boost it to 18, which is same as boots of 
speed. Ki-rin have a base speed of 18; I don't know if it can be boosted 
further with a wand. Ki-rin make great steeds but require retaming once 
in a long while (as they don't eat). Dragons have a base speed of 9, 
IIRC, so even with the wand they only go up to a PC's base speed. I 
consider this too slow.

